  "id": "oral-history",
  "term": "oral history",
  "definition": "Oral history is the passing on of a group’s remembered past by spoken accounts rather than writing, serving as a form of collective memory and cultural heritage. In this source, it is closely related to oral genealogies, which can preserve recent ancestry accurately but may also change over time through inference, social or political relationships, and mythical elements.",
